{"kind":"report","text":"Finished static I3 preparation at frozen ae3ea555eca36f767568a39920a34918d0982a46 against cbb4cc180efc9c6cdea9c9b5747bd873022360ee. This completes checker-owned preparation 4417edbb, not an ordinary source verdict or an I3 milestone.\n\nCoverage: five independent readers collectively read all 65 changed/new current subjects (1,056,193 bytes / 17,083 LF) and every assigned addition, removal and context byte through EOF. Fresh whole-body reading was used except eight same-reader, exact-identity-verified prior FULL transfers in n5 with FULL current deltas and affected contexts. Root read all five sealed ledgers/reports through EOF, independently matched all65 current metadata and prior blob identities, all27 declared prior-text identities, all five complete delta hashes, and all14 driver evidence-file hashes: zero mismatches, omissions or duplicate assignments. Root personally read full authority.ts, operations.ts, grant.ts, current contract-deltas and evidence.ts, plus the relevant SQLite, turn, ledger, bytes and repaired plan clauses; no root-personal FULL65 or fresh whole-plan claim. Binding /tmp/artroom-checker-i3-ae3-preparation-binding.json, 42,386 bytes, SHA256 7e48253ad6b9a1d4665a394822d931f6667d5961e00aaca02feb99f5cec8ee50.\n\nThree P2 component implementation findings, to resolve under existing I3 owner duties before real opening/owner integration:\n1. Reconsider all parked attempts on restart. operations.ts171–172 clears #first after one deliveryBatch query; sqlite.ts321–326 has no parked cursor and excludes null-next rows from later queries/alarms. More than one parked batch strands later rows; an unsupported oldest batch can starve supported later rows on every restart, and unrelated due rows can consume the startup batch. Use a finite bounded startup walk with an advancing cursor and a wake while pages remain; preserve unsupported parking and the durable no-second-send mark.\n2. Retain an internal late answer across temporary turn